# Assign this batch to fixed global themes

The JSON input contains global group identifiers, labels and scope boundaries established from the entire source collection, followed by one bounded batch of unchanged source items.

Assign EVERY item identifier in this batch to exactly one existing integer group identifier.
Interpret each item as a whole and choose its main substantive meaning.
For mixed items, apply the supplied theme boundaries consistently.
Do not invent a group, alter the themes, sort by identifier, duplicate an item or leave an item unassigned.

Return only the requested JSON assignments object.
Do not repeat, paraphrase or copy the source strings.
The caller uses the identifiers to reconstruct each complete original string exactly once.
A group may have no member in this batch; the global partition, not each individual batch, uses all groups.
